{"type":"message","id":"assistant-aa2b508500","parentId":"user-aa2b508500","timestamp":"2026-06-19T03:50:18.000Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants a complete, highly realistic 3D model of the Taj Mahal with surrounding scenery, a free‑view camera system, and a polished 20‑second cinematic showcase. I have already confirmed that the project directory is empty, so I need to create all necessary files from scratch. Since this is a self‑contained web demo, the simplest approach is to generate a single `index.html` that includes all HTML, CSS, and JavaScript (using ES modules) needed to build the scene with Three.js.\n\nFirst, I should decide on the structure of the HTML file:\n- A minimal `<head>` with meta tags, a title, and a `<style>` block for full‑screen layout, HUD, play button, cinematic bars, vignette, title cards, and fade overlay.\n- An `<importmap>` to load Three.js from a CDN (so I don’t have to bundle anything locally) and map the `three/addons/` path for controls, sky, and reflector.\n- In the `<body>`, placeholders for the app container, vignette, HUD, play button, top/bottom bars, title cards, and fader.\n- A `<script type=\"module\">` that imports Three.js and the necessary addons, then constructs the scene.\n\nNext, I need to flesh out the script. The user expects a “most realistic and accurate” model, so I will procedurally generate the major architectural elements (plinth, pishtaqs, onion dome, chhatris, minarets, mosque & jawab, gate, charbagh garden, water, trees). I’ll define helper functions:\n- `M` to create a mesh with position and shadow settings.\n- `noiseTexture` to generate procedural marble, sandstone, grass, and path textures using a canvas.\n- Functions for onion dome (`onionDome`), finial (`finial`), chhatri (`chhatri`), arch path (`archPath`), arched panel (`archedPanel`), guldasta (`guldasta`), and minaret (`minaret`).\nThese will let me assemble the monument without external assets, satisfying the “no mistakes” requirement.\n\nI also need realistic lighting: a skybox using `Sky`, a directional sun positioned for golden hour, a hemisphere light, and a bounce light. Shadows should be enabled with a high-resolution shadow map.\n\nThe camera system must support both orbit controls and a fly mode. I’ll instantiate `OrbitControls`, configure damping, limits, and target. Then I’ll add a custom fly controller that toggles with the `F` key, locks the pointer, and processes WASD/QE movement with speed boost.\n\nFor the cinematic showcase, I’ll script a 20‑second sequence:\n- Define key positions (`camKeys`) and look‑at points (`lookKeys`).\n- Use `CatmullRomCurve3` for smooth interpolation.\n- Create a `showcase` object with playback state, and functions `startShowcase`, `endShowcase`, and `updateShowcase`.\n- Include title cards, cinematic bars, and a fade overlay, all controlled via CSS classes.\n- Add cues for title in/out and end card.\n\nI’ll also add small atmospheric details: birds (simple wing geometry animated), a reflecting water surface using `Reflector`, trees (cypress and orchard) placed with pseudo‑randomness, and perimeter walls.\n\nFinally, the main animation loop will update birds, the showcase (or fly mode or orbit controls), and render the scene. A resize handler will keep the canvas full‑screen.\n\nAll of this code can be placed directly into the HTML file. The user asked for the final product to be a single `index.html`, so I will write the entire content to `C:\\Users\\aranr\\CascadeProjects\\3d-render\\index.html`. The content must start with the `<!DOCTYPE html>` declaration and include everything described above.\n\nThus, the next step is to issue a Write tool call with the exact file path and the full HTML content I have just assembled."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_aa2b5085002e37a7","name":"Write","arguments":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\aranr\\CascadeProjects\\3d-render\\index.html","content":"<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n<title>Taj Mahal — A Dream in Marble</title>\n<style>\n  html, body { margin: 0; padding: 0; overflow: hidden; background: #000; height: 100%; }\n  #app { position: fixed; inset: 0; }\n  canvas { display: block; }\n\n  /* ---------- HUD ---------- */\n  #hud {\n    position: fixed; top: 18px; left: 18px; z-index: 10;\n    color: #f3ead8; font-family: 'Segoe UI', system-ui, sans-serif;\n    text-shadow: 0 1px 6px rgba(0,0,0,.7);\n    user-select: none; pointer-events: none;\n    transition: opacity .6s ease;\n  }\n  #hud h1 { font-size: 19px; margin: 0 0 6px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 3px; }\n  #hud p  { font-size: 12px; margin: 2px 0; opacity: .82; line-height: 1.5; }\n  #hud kbd {\n    background: rgba(255,255,255,.14); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.25);\n    border-radius: 4px; padding: 0 5px; font-size: 11px; font-family: inherit;\n  }\n\n  #playBtn {\n    position: fixed; bottom: 26px; left: 50%; transform: translateX(-50%); z-index: 10;\n    background: rgba(20, 16, 12, .55); color: #f6edd9;\n    border: 1px solid rgba(246, 237, 217, .45); border-radius: 30px;\n    padding: 12px 30px; font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: 2.5px;\n    font-family: 'Segoe UI', system-ui, sans-serif; cursor: pointer;\n    backdrop-filter: blur(6px); transition: all .25s ease;\n  }\n  #playBtn:hover { background: rgba(246,237,217,.92); color: #2a1f14; }\n  .hidden { opacity: 0 !important; pointer-events: none !important; }\n\n  /* ---------- Cinematic overlay ---------- */\n  #barTop, #barBot {\n    position: fixed; left: 0; right: 0; height: 0; background: #000; z-index: 20;\n    transition: height 1.2s cubic-bezier(.65,0,.35,1);\n  }\n  #barTop { top: 0; } #barBot { bottom: 0; }\n  .bars-on #barTop, .bars-on #barBot { height: 11vh; }\n\n  #vignette {\n    position: fixed; inset: 0; pointer-events: none; z-index: 5;\n    background: radial-gradient(ellipse at center, transparent 58%, rgba(0,0,0,.38) 100%);\n  }\n\n  .title-card {\n    position: fixed; left: 0; right: 0; text-align: center; z-index: 21;\n    color: #f7efdd; font-family: Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;\n    pointer-events: none; opacity: 0; transition: opacity 1.6s ease;\n    text-shadow: 0 2px 18px rgba(0,0,0,.8);\n  }\n  #titleMain { top: 16vh; }\n  #titleMain .big { font-size: clamp(34px, 6vw, 74px); letter-spacing: 14px; font-weight: 400; }\n  #titleMain .sub { font-size: clamp(12px, 1.4vw, 17px); letter-spacing: 6px; opacity: .85; margin-top: 10px; font-style: italic; }\n  #titleEnd { bottom: 15vh; }\n  #titleEnd .big { font-size: clamp(16px, 2.2vw, 26px); letter-spacing: 8px; }\n  #titleEnd .sub { font-size: clamp(11px, 1.2vw, 14px); letter-spacing: 4px; opacity: .8; margin-top: 8px; }\n  .visible { opacity: 1 !important; }\n\n  #fader { position: fixed; inset: 0; background: #000; z-index: 30; pointer-events: none;\n           opacity: 0; transition: opacity 1.1s ease; }\n</style>\n<script type=\"importmap\">\n{\n  \"imports\": {\n    \"three\": \"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.160.0/build/three.module.js\",\n    \"three/addons/\": \"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.160.0/examples/jsm/\"\n  }\n}\n</script>\n</head>\n<body>\n<div id=\"app\"></div>\n<div id=\"vignette\"></div>\n\n<div id=\"hud\">\n  <h1>TAJ MAHAL</h1>\n  <p>Drag to orbit &nbsp;·&nbsp; Scroll to zoom &nbsp;·&nbsp; Right-drag to pan</p>\n  <p><kbd>F</kbd> fly mode (<kbd>W</kbd><kbd>A</kbd><kbd>S</kbd><kbd>D</kbd> move, <kbd>Q</kbd><kbd>E</kbd> down/up, <kbd>Shift</kbd> fast, <kbd>Esc</kbd> exit)</p>\n  <p><kbd>Space</kbd> play the cinematic showcase</p>\n</div>\n<button id=\"playBtn\">▶ &nbsp;CINEMATIC SHOWCASE</button>\n\n<div id=\"barTop\"></div><div id=\"barBot\"></div>\n<div id=\"titleMain\" class=\"title-card\">\n  <div class=\"big\">TAJ MAHAL</div>\n  <div class=\"sub\">a teardrop on the cheek of time</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"titleEnd\" class=\"title-card\">\n  <div class=\"big\">AGRA &nbsp;·&nbsp; INDIA</div>\n  <div class=\"sub\">built 1632 – 1653 &nbsp;·&nbsp; rendered in WebGL</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"fader\"></div>\n\n<script type=\"module\">\nimport * as THREE from 'three';\nimport { OrbitControls } from 'three/addons/controls/OrbitControls.js';\nimport { Sky } from 'three/addons/objects/Sky.js';\nimport { Reflector } from 'three/addons/objects/Reflector.js';\n\n/* ================================================================\n   RENDERER / SCENE / CAMERA\n   ================================================================ */\nconst renderer = new THREE.WebGLRenderer({ antialias: true });\nrenderer.setSize(window.innerWidth, window.innerHeight);\nrenderer.setPixelRatio(Math.min(window.devicePixelRatio, 2));\nrenderer.shadowMap.enabled = true;\nrenderer.shadowMap.type = THREE.PCFSoftShadowMap;\nrenderer.toneMapping = THREE.ACESFilmicToneMapping;\nrenderer.toneMappingExposure = 0.62;\ndocument.getElementById('app').appendChild(renderer.domElement);\n\nconst scene = new THREE.Scene();\nscene.fog = new THREE.FogExp2(0xe8c9a6, 0.00085);\n\nconst camera = new THREE.PerspectiveCamera(52, window.innerWidth / window.innerHeight, 0.5, 4000);\ncamera.position.set(95, 42, 130);\n\n/* Monument center (the mausoleum sits at the river end of the garden) */\nconst MC = new THREE.Vector3(0, 0, -120);\n\n/* ================================================================\n   SKY & LIGHTING  (golden hour)\n   ================================================================ */\nconst sky = new Sky();\nsky.scale.setScalar(20000);\nscene.add(sky);\nconst skyU = sky.material.uniforms;\nskyU.turbidity.value = 5.5;\nskyU.rayleigh.value = 2.4;\nskyU.mieCoefficient.value = 0.006;\nskyU.mieDirectionalG.value = 0.82;\n\nconst sunDir = new THREE.Vector3();\n{\n  const elev = THREE.MathUtils.degToRad(13);      // low golden sun\n  const azim = THREE.MathUtils.degToRad(212);     // from the south-west, raking the facade\n  sunDir.setFromSphericalCoords(1, Math.PI / 2 - elev, azim);\n  skyU.sunPosition.value.copy(sunDir);\n}\n\nconst sun = new THREE.DirectionalLight(0xffd9a8, 3.1);\nsun.position.copy(sunDir).multiplyScalar(600).add(MC);\nsun.target.position.copy(MC);\nsun.castShadow = true;\nsun.shadow.mapSize.set(4096, 4096);\nsun.shadow.camera.near = 50;\nsun.shadow.camera.far = 1400;\nconst D = 260;\nsun.shadow.camera.left = -D; sun.shadow.camera.right = D;\nsun.shadow.camera.top = D;   sun.shadow.camera.bottom = -D;\nsun.shadow.bias = -0.0004;\nscene.add(sun, sun.target);\n\nscene.add(new THREE.HemisphereLight(0xcfd9ff, 0x6e5a44, 0.85));\nconst bounce = new THREE.DirectionalLight(0x9fb4d8, 0.5);      // cool sky bounce from the north\nbounce.position.set(-200, 180, -500);\nscene.add(bounce);\n\n/* ================================================================\n   TEXTURE HELPERS (procedural canvases — no external assets)\n   ================================================================ */\nfunction noiseTexture(base, grain, repeat, alpha = 18) {\n  const c = document.createElement('canvas'); c.width = c.height = 256;\n  const g = c.getContext('2d');\n  g.fillStyle = base; g.fillRect(0, 0, 256, 256);\n  for (let i = 0; i < 2600; i++) {\n    g.fillStyle = `rgba(${grain},${Math.random() * alpha / 100})`;\n    g.fillRect(Math.random() * 256, Math.random() * 256, 2, 2);\n  }\n  const t = new THREE.CanvasTexture(c);\n  t.wrapS = t.wrapT = THREE.RepeatWrapping;\n  t.repeat.set(repeat, repeat);\n  t.colorSpace = THREE.SRGBColorSpace;\n  return t;\n}\n\nconst marbleMat = new THREE.MeshPhysicalMaterial({\n  color: 0xf2ead9, roughness: 0.42, metalness: 0.0,\n  clearcoat: 0.25, clearcoatRoughness: 0.5, sheen: 0.3, sheenColor: 0xfff4dd\n});\nconst marbleDarkMat = new THREE.MeshStandardMaterial({ color: 0x5a4f40, roughness: 0.55 });\nconst recessMat = new THREE.MeshStandardMaterial({ color: 0x2e2620, roughness: 0.92 });\nconst sandstoneMat = new THREE.MeshStandardMaterial({\n  map: noiseTexture('#a9543a', '40,20,15', 8, 30), color: 0xffffff, roughness: 0.9\n});\nconst pathMat = new THREE.MeshStandardMaterial({\n  map: noiseTexture('#b98a62', '70,50,35', 14, 25), roughness: 0.95\n});\nconst grassMat = new THREE.MeshStandardMaterial({\n  map: noiseTexture('#4d6b34', '25,40,18', 26, 35), roughness: 1.0\n});\nconst goldMat = new THREE.MeshStandardMaterial({ color: 0xd8a93f, metalness: 0.9, roughness: 0.32 });\nconst leafMat = new THREE.MeshStandardMaterial({ color: 0x2f4a26, roughness: 0.95 });\nconst leafMat2 = new THREE.MeshStandardMaterial({ color: 0x44632f, roughness: 0.95 });\nconst trunkMat = new THREE.MeshStandardMaterial({ color: 0x5b4632, roughness: 0.95 });\n\nfunction M(geo, mat, x = 0, y = 0, z = 0, shadow = true) {\n  const m = new THREE.Mesh(geo, mat);\n  m.position.set(x, y, z);\n  m.castShadow = shadow; m.receiveShadow = true;\n  return m;\n}\n\n/* ================================================================\n   ARCHITECTURAL PIECES\n   ================================================================ */\n\n/* --- Onion dome via lathe. r = max radius, h = height of dome body --- */\nfunction onionDome(r, h, mat = marbleMat) {\n  const pts = [];\n  const prof = [           // [radiusFactor, heightFactor]\n    [0.62, 0.00], [0.80, 0.04], [0.93, 0.12], [1.00, 0.26], [0.99, 0.40],\n    [0.92, 0.55], [0.78, 0.68], [0.58, 0.79], [0.38, 0.875], [0.20, 0.935],\n    [0.075, 0.975], [0.0, 1.0]\n  ];\n  for (const [rf, hf] of prof) pts.push(new THREE.Vector2(rf * r, hf * h));\n  const dome = new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.LatheGeometry(pts, 48), mat);\n  dome.castShadow = true; dome.receiveShadow = true;\n  return dome;\n}\n\n/* --- Gold finial spire --- */\nfunction finial(h) {\n  const g = new THREE.Group();\n  g.add(M(new THREE.CylinderGeometry(0.10 * h, 0.16 * h, 0.5 * h, 12), goldMat, 0, 0.25 * h, 0));\n  g.add(M(new THREE.SphereGeometry(0.13 * h, 12, 10), goldMat, 0, 0.42 * h, 0));\n  g.add(M(new THREE.SphereGeometry(0.10 * h, 12, 10), goldMat, 0, 0.62 * h, 0));\n  g.add(M(new THREE.SphereGeometry(0.075 * h, 10, 8), goldMat, 0, 0.78 * h, 0));\n  g.add(M(new THREE.ConeGeometry(0.045 * h, 0.28 * h, 10), goldMat, 0, 0.97 * h, 0));\n  const moon = M(new THREE.TorusGeometry(0.09 * h, 0.018 * h, 8, 24, Math.PI * 1.25), goldMat, 0, 1.08 * h, 0);\n  moon.rotation.z = Math.PI * 0.62;\n  g.add(moon);\n  return g;\n}\n\n/* --- Chhatri: open domed kiosk on slender columns --- */\nfunction chhatri(radius, colH, mat = marbleMat) {\n  const g = new THREE.Group();\n  const n = 8;\n  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n    const a = (i / n) * Math.PI * 2;\n    g.add(M(new THREE.CylinderGeometry(radius * 0.075, radius * 0.09, colH, 10),\n            mat, Math.cos(a) * radius * 0.82, colH / 2, Math.sin(a) * radius * 0.82));\n  }\n  g.add(M(new THREE.CylinderGeometry(radius * 1.06, radius * 1.06, radius * 0.16, 8), mat, 0, colH + radius * 0.08, 0)); // entablature\n  g.add(M(new THREE.CylinderGeometry(radius * 1.14, radius * 1.14, radius * 0.07, 8), mat, 0, colH + radius * 0.20, 0)); // chajja (eave)\n  g.add(M(new THREE.CylinderGeometry(radius * 0.05, radius * 1.0, radius * 0.1, 8), mat, 0, colH - radius * 0.05 + radius * 0.21, 0));\n  const dome = onionDome(radius * 0.82, radius * 1.05, mat);\n  dome.position.y = colH + radius * 0.24;\n  g.add(dome);\n  const fin = finial(radius * 0.8);\n  fin.position.y = colH + radius * 0.24 + radius * 1.02;\n  g.add(fin);\n  g.add(M(new THREE.CylinderGeometry(radius * 0.95, radius * 1.0, 0.3, 8), mat, 0, 0.15, 0)); // base slab\n  return g;\n}\n\n/* --- Pointed (Mughal) arch outline for shapes --- */\nfunction archPath(path, w, h, dir = 1) {\n  // draws up one side, over the point, down the other; w = half-width, h = total height\n  const spring = h * 0.55;          // where the curve starts\n  path.lineTo(-w * dir, 0);\n  path.lineTo(-w * dir, spring);\n  path.quadraticCurveTo(-w * dir, h * 0.86, -w * 0.42 * dir, h * 0.955);\n  path.quadraticCurveTo(-w * 0.12 * dir, h * 1.0, 0, h);\n  path.quadraticCurveTo(w * 0.12 * dir, h * 1.0, w * 0.42 * dir, h * 0.955);\n  path.quadraticCurveTo(w * dir, h * 0.86, w * dir, spring);\n  path.lineTo(w * dir, 0);\n}\n\n/* --- Arched panel: marble frame with a pointed-arch recess + dark inset --- */\nfunction archedPanel(W, H, depth, archHalfW, archH, opts = {}) {\n  const g = new THREE.Group();\n  const shape = new THREE.Shape();\n  shape.moveTo(-W / 2, 0); shape.lineTo(W / 2, 0);\n  shape.lineTo(W / 2, H); shape.lineTo(-W / 2, H); shape.closePath();\n\n  const hole = new THREE.Path();\n  hole.moveTo(-archHalfW, 0);\n  archPath(hole, -archHalfW, archH, -1);   // build the arch hole (wound consistently)\n  shape.holes.push(hole);\n\n  const frame = new THREE.Mesh(\n    new THREE.ExtrudeGeometry(shape, { depth, bevelEnabled: false }), opts.mat || marbleMat);\n  frame.castShadow = true; frame.receiveShadow = true;\n  g.add(frame);\n\n  // dark recessed interior behind the arch\n  const inner = M(new THREE.BoxGeometry(archHalfW * 2, archH, 0.4), recessMat,\n                  0, archH / 2, depth * 0.18);\n  g.add(inner);\n\n  // pietra-dura style border band around the arch\n  if (opts.band !== false) {\n    const bandShape = new THREE.Shape();\n    const bw = archHalfW * 1.22, bh = archH * 1.1;\n    bandShape.moveTo(-bw, 0);\n    archPath(bandShape, -bw, bh, -1);\n    bandShape.closePath();\n    const bandHole = new THREE.Path();\n    bandHole.moveTo(-archHalfW * 1.06, 0);\n    archPath(bandHole, -archHalfW * 1.06, archH * 1.03, -1);\n    bandShape.holes.push(bandHole);\n    const band = new THREE.Mesh(\n      new THREE.ExtrudeGeometry(bandShape, { depth: 0.12, bevelEnabled: false }), marbleDarkMat);\n    band.position.z = depth + 0.01;\n    g.add(band);\n  }\n  return g;\n}\n\n/* --- Slender corner pinnacle (guldasta) --- */\nfunction guldasta(h) {\n  const g = new THREE.Group();\n  g.add(M(new THREE.CylinderGeometry(0.32, 0.45, h, 10), marbleMat, 0, h / 2, 0));\n  g.add(M(new THREE.SphereGeometry(0.55, 12, 10), marbleMat, 0, h + 0.3, 0));\n  const f = finial(1.6); f.position.y = h + 0.6; g.add(f);\n  return g;\n}\n\n/* ================================================================\n   THE MAUSOLEUM\n   ================================================================ */\nconst taj = new THREE.Group();\ntaj.position.copy(MC);\nscene.add(taj);\n\nconst TERRACE_TOP = 1.4;     // red sandstone riverfront terrace\nconst PLINTH_H = 6.8;\nconst PLINTH_TOP = TERRACE_TOP + PLINTH_H;   // 8.2\nconst BODY_H = 25;\nconst ROOF_Y = PLINTH_TOP + BODY_H;          // 33.2\n\n/* --- riverfront terrace --- */\n{\n  const t = M(new THREE.BoxGeometry(300, TERRACE_TOP, 120), sandstoneMat, 0, TERRACE_TOP / 2, 0);\n  taj.add(t);\n}\n\n/* --- marble plinth (95 × 95) --- */\n{\n  const p = M(new THREE.BoxGeometry(95, PLINTH_H, 95), marbleMat, 0, TERRACE_TOP + PLINTH_H / 2, 0);\n  taj.add(p);\n  // moulding lip\n  taj.add(M(new THREE.BoxGeometry(97, 0.9, 97), marbleMat, 0, PLINTH_TOP - 0.45, 0));\n  // staircase block on the garden (south, +z) side\n  for (let i = 0; i < 7; i++) {\n    taj.add(M(new THREE.BoxGeometry(16, PLINTH_H / 7, 2.2),\n              marbleMat, 0, TERRACE_TOP + PLINTH_H / 14 + i * PLINTH_H / 7, 47.5 + (6 - i) * 1.1 + 1.1));\n  }\n}\n\n/* --- main body: square with chamfered corners (irregular octagon) --- */\nconst HALF = 28.5, CH = 12;   // 57 m wide, 12 m chamfers\n{\n  const s = new THREE.Shape();\n  s.moveTo(-HALF + CH, -HALF); s.lineTo(HALF - CH, -HALF);\n  s.lineTo(HALF, -HALF + CH);  s.lineTo(HALF, HALF - CH);\n  s.lineTo(HALF - CH, HALF);   s.lineTo(-HALF + CH, HALF);\n  s.lineTo(-HALF, HALF - CH);  s.lineTo(-HALF, -HALF + CH);\n  s.closePath();\n  const body = new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.ExtrudeGeometry(s, { depth: BODY_H, bevelEnabled: false }), marbleMat);\n  body.rotation.x = -Math.PI / 2;\n  body.position.y = PLINTH_TOP + BODY_H;\n  body.castShadow = true; body.receiveShadow = true;\n  taj.add(body);\n\n  // parapet\n  const ps = new THREE.Shape();\n  const PH = HALF + 0.7, PC = CH;\n  ps.moveTo(-PH + PC, -PH); ps.lineTo(PH - PC, -PH); ps.lineTo(PH, -PH + PC); ps.lineTo(PH, PH - PC);\n  ps.lineTo(PH - PC, PH); ps.lineTo(-PH + PC, PH); ps.lineTo(-PH, PH - PC); ps.lineTo(-PH, -PH + PC);\n  ps.closePath();\n  const hole = new THREE.Path();\n  const IH = HALF - 1.4, IC = CH;\n  hole.moveTo(-IH + IC, -IH); hole.lineTo(-IH, -IH + IC); hole.lineTo(-IH, IH - IC); hole.lineTo(-IH + IC, IH);\n  hole.lineTo(IH - IC, IH); hole.lineTo(IH, IH - IC); hole.lineTo(IH, -IH + IC); hole.lineTo(IH - IC, -IH);\n  hole.closePath();\n  ps.holes.push(hole);\n  const parapet = new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.ExtrudeGeometry(ps, { depth: 1.8, bevelEnabled: false }), marbleMat);\n  parapet.rotation.x = -Math.PI / 2;\n  parapet.position.y = ROOF_Y + 1.8;\n  parapet.castShadow = true; parapet.receiveShadow = true;\n  taj.add(parapet);\n}\n\n/* --- four grand pishtaqs (iwan portals), one per facade --- */\n{\n  const PW = 23, PHT = 32.5, PD = 2.6;\n  const sides = [\n    { x: 0, z: HALF, ry: 0 }, { x: 0, z: -HALF, ry: Math.PI },\n    { x: HALF, z: 0, ry: Math.PI / 2 }, { x: -HALF, z: 0, ry: -Math.PI / 2 }\n  ];\n  for (const sd of sides) {\n    const p = archedPanel(PW, PHT, PD, 7.2, 24);\n    p.position.set(sd.x, PLINTH_TOP, sd.z);\n    p.rotation.y = sd.ry;\n    taj.add(p);\n    // crown of the pishtaq frame + small guldastas\n    const top = M(new THREE.BoxGeometry(PW + 1.2, 1.6, PD + 1), marbleMat);\n    top.position.set(sd.x, PLINTH_TOP + PHT + 0.8, sd.z);\n    top.rotation.y = sd.ry;\n    top.translateZ(PD / 2);\n    taj.add(top);\n    for (const off of [-PW / 2, PW / 2]) {\n      const gd = guldasta(3.4);\n      gd.position.set(sd.x, PLINTH_TOP + PHT + 1.4, sd.z);\n      gd.rotation.y = sd.ry;\n      gd.translateX(off);\n      taj.add(gd);\n    }\n    // two-story flanking niches\n    for (const sideOff of [-HALF + CH / 2 + 8.2, HALF - CH / 2 - 8.2]) {\n      for (const lvl of [0, BODY_H / 2]) {\n        const n = archedPanel(8.6, BODY_H / 2 - 1.2, 1.2, 2.9, 9.5, { band: false });\n        n.position.set(sd.x, PLINTH_TOP + lvl + 0.6, sd.z);\n        n.rotation.y = sd.ry;\n        n.translateX(sideOff * (Math.abs(sd.z) > 0 ? 1 : 1));\n        taj.add(n);\n      }\n    }\n  }\n  // chamfer-corner niches\n  const corners = [\n    { x: HALF - CH / 2, z: HALF - CH / 2, ry: Math.PI / 4 },\n    { x: -(HALF - CH / 2), z: HALF - CH / 2, ry: -Math.PI / 4 },\n    { x: HALF - CH / 2, z: -(HALF - CH / 2), ry: Math.PI * 3 / 4 },\n    { x: -(HALF - CH / 2), z: -(HALF - CH / 2), ry: -Math.PI * 3 / 4 }\n  ];\n  for (const c of corners) {\n    for (const lvl of [0, BODY_H / 2]) {\n      const n = archedPanel(10.5, BODY_H / 2 - 1.2, 1.3, 3.4, 10, { band: false });\n      n.position.set(c.x, PLINTH_TOP + lvl + 0.6, c.z);\n      n.rotation.y = c.ry;\n      taj.add(n);\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n/* --- central drum + great onion dome --- */\n{\n  taj.add(M(new THREE.CylinderGeometry(10.6, 10.9, 8, 40), marbleMat, 0, ROOF_Y + 4, 0));\n  taj.add(M(new THREE.CylinderGeometry(11.3, 11.3, 1.2, 40), marbleMat, 0, ROOF_Y + 8.4, 0)); // drum cornice\n  // ring of lotus petals at dome base\n  for (let i = 0; i < 24; i++) {\n    const a = (i / 24) * Math.PI * 2;\n    const petal = M(new THREE.ConeGeometry(0.9, 2.4, 6), marbleMat,\n                    Math.cos(a) * 10.9, ROOF_Y + 9.6, Math.sin(a) * 10.9);\n    taj.add(petal);\n  }\n  const dome = onionDome(11.6, 19.5);\n  dome.position.y = ROOF_Y + 9;\n  taj.add(dome);\n  const f = finial(9.5);\n  f.position.y = ROOF_Y + 9 + 19.3;\n  taj.add(f);\n}\n\n/* --- four chhatris around the dome --- */\nfor (const [cx, cz] of [[17.5, 17.5], [-17.5, 17.5], [17.5, -17.5], [-17.5, -17.5]]) {\n  const ch = chhatri(4.6, 6.2);\n  ch.position.set(cx, ROOF_Y, cz);\n  taj.add(ch);\n}\n/* guldastas at the chamfer roof edges */\nfor (const [gx, gz] of [\n  [HALF - CH / 2 + 2, HALF - CH / 2 + 2], [-(HALF - CH / 2 + 2), HALF - CH / 2 + 2],\n  [HALF - CH / 2 + 2, -(HALF - CH / 2 + 2)], [-(HALF - CH / 2 + 2), -(HALF - CH / 2 + 2)]\n]) {\n  const g = guldasta(5);\n  g.position.set(gx * 0.92, ROOF_Y, gz * 0.92);\n  taj.add(g);\n}\n\n/* ================================================================\n   FOUR MINARETS (at plinth corners)\n   ================================================================ */\nfunction minaret() {\n  const g = new THREE.Group();\n  const H = 40;\n  g.add(M(new THREE.CylinderGeometry(3.6, 4.1, 1.6, 8), marbleMat, 0, 0.8, 0)); // octagonal base\n  g.add(M(new THREE.CylinderGeometry(1.85, 2.7, H, 20), marbleMat, 0, 1.6 + H / 2, 0));\n  // three balconies\n  for (const by of [0.34, 0.62, 0.88]) {\n    const y = 1.6 + H * by;\n    const r = THREE.MathUtils.lerp(2.7, 1.85, by) + 1.0;\n    g.add(M(new THREE.CylinderGeometry(r, r * 0.82, 0.5, 16), marbleMat, 0, y, 0));\n    g.add(M(new THREE.TorusGeometry(r * 0.96, 0.14, 8, 24), marbleDarkMat, 0, y + 0.55, 0))\n      .children?.at?.(-1);\n    const rail = M(new THREE.CylinderGeometry(r * 0.99, r * 0.99, 0.9, 16, 1, true),\n                   marbleMat, 0, y + 0.7, 0);\n    rail.material = new THREE.MeshStandardMaterial({\n      color: 0xf2ead9, roughness: 0.5, side: THREE.DoubleSide, transparent: true, opacity: 0.9\n    });\n    g.add(rail);\n  }\n  const top = chhatri(2.5, 3.4);\n  top.position.y = 1.6 + H;\n  g.add(top);\n  return g;\n}\nfor (const [mx, mz] of [[43, 43], [-43, 43], [43, -43], [-43, -43]]) {\n  const m = minaret();\n  m.position.set(mx, PLINTH_TOP, mz);\n  taj.add(m);\n}\n\n/* ================================================================\n   MOSQUE (west) & JAWAB (east) — red sandstone, three white domes\n   ================================================================ */\nfunction sideBuilding() {\n  const g = new THREE.Group();\n  const W = 56, Hh = 14, Dd = 20;\n  g.add(M(new THREE.BoxGeometry(W, Hh, Dd), sandstoneMat, 0, Hh / 2, 0));\n  // central pishtaq\n  const p = archedPanel(16, 19, 2, 5, 14, { mat: sandstoneMat, band: false });\n  p.position.set(0, 0, Dd / 2);\n  g.add(p);\n  for (const off of [-19, 19]) {\n    const n = archedPanel(10, 11, 1.4, 3.2, 8.5, { mat: sandstoneMat, band: false });\n    n.position.set(off, 0, Dd / 2);\n    g.add(n);\n  }\n  // three marble domes on drums\n  for (const [dx, ds] of [[0, 1.0], [-19, 0.78], [19, 0.78]]) {\n    g.add(M(new THREE.CylinderGeometry(5.6 * ds, 5.8 * ds, 3, 24), marbleMat, dx, Hh + 1.5, 0));\n    const d = onionDome(6.1 * ds, 9.5 * ds);\n    d.position.set(dx, Hh + 3, 0);\n    g.add(d);\n    const f = finial(4 * ds);\n    f.position.set(dx, Hh + 3 + 9.4 * ds, 0);\n    g.add(f);\n  }\n  // corner turrets\n  for (const tx of [-W / 2, W / 2]) for (const tz of [-Dd / 2, Dd / 2]) {\n    g.add(M(new THREE.CylinderGeometry(1.3, 1.5, Hh + 3, 10), sandstoneMat, tx, (Hh + 3) / 2, tz));\n    const c = chhatri(1.7, 2.2);\n    c.position.set(tx, Hh + 3, tz);\n    g.add(c);\n  }\n  return g;\n}\n{\n  const mosque = sideBuilding();\n  mosque.position.set(-118, TERRACE_TOP, -120);\n  mosque.rotation.y = -Math.PI / 2;   // faces the mausoleum\n  scene.add(mosque);\n  const jawab = sideBuilding();\n  jawab.position.set(118, TERRACE_TOP, -120);\n  jawab.rotation.y = Math.PI / 2;\n  scene.add(jawab);\n  // sandstone platforms under them\n  scene.add(M(new THREE.BoxGeometry(34, 1.4, 70), sandstoneMat, -118, TERRACE_TOP + 0.7 - 1.4, -120));\n  scene.add(M(new THREE.BoxGeometry(34, 1.4, 70), sandstoneMat, 118, TERRACE_TOP + 0.7 - 1.4, -120));\n}\n\n/* ================================================================\n   GREAT GATE (Darwaza-i-Rauza, south end of the garden)\n   ================================================================ */\n{\n  const gate = new THREE.Group();\n  const W = 42, Hh = 21, Dd = 16;\n  gate.add(M(new THREE.BoxGeometry(W, Hh, Dd), sandstoneMat, 0, Hh / 2, 0));\n  // grand iwan facing the garden (north, -z side)\n  const p1 = archedPanel(20, 26, 2.4, 6.4, 19);\n  p1.position.set(0, 0, -Dd / 2 - 2.4);\n  gate.add(p1);\n  const p2 = archedPanel(20, 26, 2.4, 6.4, 19);\n  p2.position.set(0, 0, Dd / 2 + 2.4);\n  p2.rotation.y = Math.PI;\n  gate.add(p2);\n  // row of eleven mini chhatris along the top\n  for (let i = 0; i < 11; i++) {\n    const c = chhatri(1.35, 1.9);\n    c.position.set(-15 + i * 3, Hh, -Dd / 2 + 1.6);\n    gate.add(c);\n  }\n  // corner octagonal towers with white chhatris\n  for (const tx of [-W / 2 + 1, W / 2 - 1]) for (const tz of [-Dd / 2 + 1, Dd / 2 - 1]) {\n    gate.add(M(new THREE.CylinderGeometry(2.6, 3, Hh + 4, 8), sandstoneMat, tx, (Hh + 4) / 2, tz));\n    const c = chhatri(2.6, 3.2);\n    c.position.set(tx, Hh + 4, tz);\n    gate.add(c);\n  }\n  gate.position.set(0, 0, 192);\n  scene.add(gate);\n}\n\n/* ================================================================\n   CHARBAGH GARDENS, WATER, TREES\n   ================================================================ */\n/* ground */\nscene.add(M(new THREE.PlaneGeometry(900, 1000), grassMat, 0, -0.02, 50).rotateX?.(0) ?? new THREE.Object3D());\n{\n  const ground = new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.PlaneGeometry(900, 1000), grassMat);\n  ground.rotation.x = -Math.PI / 2;\n  ground.position.set(0, 0, 50);\n  ground.receiveShadow = true;\n  scene.add(ground);\n}\n\n/* river behind the monument (Yamuna) */\n{\n  const river = new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.PlaneGeometry(900, 260),\n    new THREE.MeshStandardMaterial({ color: 0x6d8fa3, roughness: 0.18, metalness: 0.45 }));\n  river.rotation.x = -Math.PI / 2;\n  river.position.set(0, -0.6, -315);\n  scene.add(river);\n  // far bank\n  const bank = new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.PlaneGeometry(900, 200),\n    new THREE.MeshStandardMaterial({ color: 0x7d7257, roughness: 1 }));\n  bank.rotation.x = -Math.PI / 2;\n  bank.position.set(0, -0.3, -540);\n  scene.add(bank);\n}\n\n/* central walkway + cross paths */\nscene.add(M(new THREE.BoxGeometry(16, 0.5, 245), pathMat, 0, 0.25, 62));\nscene.add(M(new THREE.BoxGeometry(300, 0.5, 14), pathMat, 0, 0.25, 62));\nscene.add(M(new THREE.BoxGeometry(300, 0.5, 12), pathMat, 0, 0.25, -56));\nscene.add(M(new THREE.BoxGeometry(300, 0.5, 12), pathMat, 0, 0.25, 180));\n\n/* long reflecting channel (al-Hawd al-Kawthar axis) */\nfunction waterSurface(w, len, x, y, z) {\n  const refl = new Reflector(new THREE.PlaneGeometry(w, len), {\n    clipBias: 0.003,\n    textureWidth: 1024,\n    textureHeight: 1024,\n    color: 0x9fb0b8\n  });\n  refl.rotation.x = -Math.PI / 2;\n  refl.position.set(x, y, z);\n  return refl;\n}\n{\n  // channel basin walls\n  scene.add(M(new THREE.BoxGeometry(8.4, 1.0, 232), marbleMat, 0, 0.5, 61));\n  scene.add(waterSurface(6.8, 229, 0, 1.06, 61));\n  // raised lotus tank at the crossing\n  scene.add(M(new THREE.BoxGeometry(26, 1.7, 26), marbleMat, 0, 0.85, 62));\n  scene.add(waterSurface(22, 22, 0, 1.78, 62));\n  // small fountain jets (static droplets suggestion: thin bright cones)\n  const jetMat = new THREE.MeshStandardMaterial({\n    color: 0xeef6ff, transparent: true, opacity: 0.55, roughness: 0.1\n  });\n  for (let z = -40; z <= 165; z += 14) {\n    if (Math.abs(z - 62) < 16) continue;\n    scene.add(M(new THREE.ConeGeometry(0.16, 1.6, 6), jetMat, 0, 1.9, z, false));\n  }\n}\n\n/* cypress avenue + orchard trees */\nfunction cypress(s = 1) {\n  const g = new THREE.Group();\n  g.add(M(new THREE.CylinderGeometry(0.16 * s, 0.22 * s, 1.2 * s, 8), trunkMat, 0, 0.6 * s, 0));\n  const cone = M(new THREE.ConeGeometry(1.05 * s, 7.5 * s, 10), leafMat, 0, 1.1 * s + 3.75 * s, 0);\n  g.add(cone);\n  return g;\n}\nfunction orchardTree(s = 1) {\n  const g = new THREE.Group();\n  g.add(M(new THREE.CylinderGeometry(0.3 * s, 0.42 * s, 2.6 * s, 8), trunkMat, 0, 1.3 * s, 0));\n  g.add(M(new THREE.IcosahedronGeometry(2.4 * s, 1), leafMat2, 0, 4.1 * s, 0));\n  g.add(M(new THREE.IcosahedronGeometry(1.7 * s, 1), leafMat, 1.3 * s, 3.4 * s, 0.6 * s));\n  g.add(M(new THREE.IcosahedronGeometry(1.5 * s, 1), leafMat2, -1.2 * s, 3.6 * s, -0.5 * s));\n  return g;\n}\n{\n  const rng = (a, b) => a + Math.random() * (b - a);\n  // formal cypress rows flanking the channel\n  for (let z = -42; z <= 168; z += 13) {\n    if (Math.abs(z - 62) < 17) continue;\n    for (const x of [-11.5, 11.5]) {\n      const c = cypress(rng(0.9, 1.15));\n      c.position.set(x, 0.4, z + rng(-0.5, 0.5));\n      scene.add(c);\n    }\n  }\n  // orchard quadrants\n  let seed = 7;\n  const rand = () => { seed = (seed * 16807) % 2147483647; return (seed % 1000) / 1000; };\n  for (let i = 0; i < 90; i++) {\n    const qx = (rand() > 0.5 ? 1 : -1), qz = (rand() > 0.5 ? 1 : -1);\n    const x = qx * (26 + rand() * 110);\n    const z = 62 + qz * (22 + rand() * 90);\n    if (z < -45 || z > 175) continue;\n    const t = rand() > 0.35 ? orchardTree(0.8 + rand() * 0.7) : cypress(0.8 + rand() * 0.6);\n    t.position.set(x, 0, z);\n    t.rotation.y = rand() * Math.PI * 2;\n    scene.add(t);\n  }\n}\n\n/* perimeter wall */\n{\n  const wallMat = sandstoneMat;\n  const mkWall = (w, d, x, z) => scene.add(M(new THREE.BoxGeometry(w, 5, d), wallMat, x, 2.5, z));\n  mkWall(6, 410, -155, -2);  mkWall(6, 410, 155, -2);\n  mkWall(120, 6, -95, 195);  mkWall(120, 6, 95, 195);\n}\n\n/* ================================================================\n   BIRDS — small flock circling the dome\n   ================================================================ */\nconst birds = [];\n{\n  const wingGeo = new THREE.BufferGeometry();\n  wingGeo.setAttribute('position', new THREE.BufferAttribute(new Float32Array([\n    0, 0, 0,  -1.4, 0.18, 0.42,  -1.4, 0.18, -0.42\n  ]), 3));\n  wingGeo.computeVertexNormals();\n  const birdMat = new THREE.MeshBasicMaterial({ color: 0x222222, side: THREE.DoubleSide });\n  for (let i = 0; i < 9; i++) {\n    const b = new THREE.Group();\n    const wl = new THREE.Mesh(wingGeo, birdMat);\n    const wr = new THREE.Mesh(wingGeo, birdMat);\n    wr.scale.x = -1;\n    b.add(wl, wr);\n    b.userData = {\n      r: 60 + Math.random() * 70,\n      h: 48 + Math.random() * 30,\n      speed: 0.10 + Math.random() * 0.08,\n      phase: Math.random() * Math.PI * 2,\n      flap: 6 + Math.random() * 4,\n      wl, wr\n    };\n    scene.add(b);\n    birds.push(b);\n  }\n}\n\n/* ================================================================\n   CAMERA SYSTEM — orbit + fly\n   ================================================================ */\nconst controls = new OrbitControls(camera, renderer.domElement);\ncontrols.target.set(0, 24, -118);\ncontrols.enableDamping = true;\ncontrols.dampingFactor = 0.06;\ncontrols.maxPolarAngle = Math.PI * 0.495;\ncontrols.minDistance = 8;\ncontrols.maxDistance = 700;\ncontrols.update();\n\nconst fly = {\n  active: false, yaw: 0, pitch: 0, speed: 26,\n  keys: {}, vel: new THREE.Vector3()\n};\nfunction enterFly() {\n  fly.active = true;\n  controls.enabled = false;\n  const e = new THREE.Euler().setFromQuaternion(camera.quaternion, 'YXZ');\n  fly.yaw = e.y; fly.pitch = e.x;\n  renderer.domElement.requestPointerLock();\n}\nfunction exitFly() {\n  fly.active = false;\n  controls.enabled = !showcase.playing;\n  if (document.pointerLockElement) document.exitPointerLock();\n  // re-aim orbit target along current view\n  const dir = new THREE.Vector3();\n  camera.getWorldDirection(dir);\n  controls.target.copy(camera.position).addScaledVector(dir, 60);\n  controls.update();\n}\ndocument.addEventListener('pointerlockchange', () => {\n  if (!document.pointerLockElement && fly.active) exitFly();\n});\ndocument.addEventListener('mousemove', (e) => {\n  if (!fly.active || !document.pointerLockElement) return;\n  fly.yaw -= e.movementX * 0.0022;\n  fly.pitch -= e.movementY * 0.0022;\n  fly.pitch = THREE.MathUtils.clamp(fly.pitch, -1.45, 1.45);\n});\nwindow.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {\n  fly.keys[e.code] = true;\n  if (e.code === 'KeyF' && !showcase.playing) fly.active ? exitFly() : enterFly();\n  if (e.code === 'Space' && !showcase.playing && !fly.active) { e.preventDefault(); startShowcase(); }\n  if (e.code === 'Escape' && showcase.playing) endShowcase(true);\n});\nwindow.addEventListener('keyup', (e) => fly.keys[e.code] = false);\n\nfunction updateFly(dt) {\n  const k = fly.keys;\n  const boost = (k['ShiftLeft'] || k['ShiftRight']) ? 3.2 : 1;\n  const dir = new THREE.Vector3();\n  if (k['KeyW']) dir.z -= 1;\n  if (k['KeyS']) dir.z += 1;\n  if (k['KeyA']) dir.x -= 1;\n  if (k['KeyD']) dir.x += 1;\n  if (k['KeyQ']) dir.y -= 1;\n  if (k['KeyE']) dir.y += 1;\n  camera.quaternion.setFromEuler(new THREE.Euler(fly.pitch, fly.yaw, 0, 'YXZ'));\n  if (dir.lengthSq() > 0) {\n    dir.normalize().applyQuaternion(camera.quaternion);\n    fly.vel.addScaledVector(dir, fly.speed * boost * dt * 6);\n  }\n  fly.vel.multiplyScalar(Math.pow(0.0008, dt));   // smooth damping\n  camera.position.addScaledVector(fly.vel, dt);\n  camera.position.y = Math.max(camera.position.y, 1.2);\n}\n\n/* ================================================================\n   THE 20-SECOND CINEMATIC SHOWCASE\n   ================================================================\n   Shot plan (director's notes):\n     0–3.5s  \"The Approach\"  — skim low over the reflecting pool from\n              the Great Gate; the Taj doubled in the water. Title in.\n     3.5–7s  \"The Rise\"      — glide past the lotus tank, lifting,\n              drifting left as the facade grows.\n     7–10.5s \"The Sweep\"     — crane around the west side past the\n              minaret, golden light raking the marble.\n    10.5–13.5s \"The Crown\"   — high behind the dome over the Yamuna,\n              the river glittering below.\n    13.5–16.5s \"The Reveal\"  — wide pull around the east, the whole\n              charbagh unfolding beneath.\n    16.5–20s \"The Rest\"      — slow settle to the classic three-quarter\n              view; bars lift; end card.\n   ================================================================ */\nconst showcase = { playing: false, t: 0, T: 20 };\n\nconst camKeys = [\n  new THREE.Vector3(0, 2.6, 178),\n  new THREE.Vector3(0, 4.5, 96),\n  new THREE.Vector3(-14, 10, 18),\n  new THREE.Vector3(-62, 22, -52),\n  new THREE.Vector3(-86, 48, -148),\n  new THREE.Vector3(-30, 80, -238),\n  new THREE.Vector3(64, 62, -196),\n  new THREE.Vector3(82, 34, -78),\n  new THREE.Vector3(34, 21, -8)\n];\nconst lookKeys = [\n  new THREE.Vector3(0, 22, -118),\n  new THREE.Vector3(0, 24, -118),\n  new THREE.Vector3(0, 28, -118),\n  new THREE.Vector3(-4, 32, -118),\n  new THREE.Vector3(0, 40, -118),\n  new THREE.Vector3(0, 38, -116),\n  new THREE.Vector3(0, 34, -118),\n  new THREE.Vector3(0, 28, -118),\n  new THREE.Vector3(0, 26, -118)\n];\nconst posCurve = new THREE.CatmullRomCurve3(camKeys, false, 'centripetal', 0.5);\nconst lookCurve = new THREE.CatmullRomCurve3(lookKeys, false, 'centripetal', 0.5);\n\nconst $ = (id) => document.getElementById(id);\nconst fired = {};\nfunction cue(name, cond, fn) { if (!fired[name] && cond) { fired[name] = true; fn(); } }\n\nfunction startShowcase() {\n  showcase.playing = true;\n  showcase.t = 0;\n  for (const k in fired) delete fired[k];\n  if (fly.active) exitFly();\n  controls.enabled = false;\n  $('hud').classList.add('hidden');\n  $('playBtn').classList.add('hidden');\n  document.body.classList.add('bars-on');\n  $('fader').style.opacity = '1';\n  setTimeout(() => $('fader').style.opacity = '0', 150);\n}\n\nfunction endShowcase(skipped = false) {\n  showcase.playing = false;\n  document.body.classList.remove('bars-on');\n  $('titleMain').classList.remove('visible');\n  $('titleEnd').classList.remove('visible');\n  $('hud').classList.remove('hidden');\n  $('playBtn').classList.remove('hidden');\n  camera.fov = 52;\n  camera.updateProjectionMatrix();\n  controls.enabled = true;\n  controls.target.set(0, 26, -118);\n  if (skipped) {\n    camera.position.set(34, 21, -8);\n  }\n  controls.update();\n}\n\nconst smooth = (x) => x * x * (3 - 2 * x);\n\nfunction updateShowcase(dt) {\n  showcase.t += dt;\n  const t = showcase.t, T = showcase.T;\n  if (t >= T) {\n    // gentle handoff: fade bars away, return control\n    endShowcase(false);\n    return;\n  }\n  let u = t / T;\n  // ease the very start and the very end, near-linear in the middle\n  const edge = 0.14;\n  let p;\n  if (u < edge)        p = smooth(u / edge) * edge;\n  else if (u > 1 - edge) p = 1 - smooth((1 - u) / edge) * edge;\n  else                 p = u;\n\n  camera.position.copy(posCurve.getPoint(p));\n  const look = lookCurve.getPoint(p);\n  camera.lookAt(look);\n\n  // slow lens tightening for the final shot\n  const f0 = 54, f1 = 44;\n  const fu = THREE.MathUtils.clamp((t - 15) / 5, 0, 1);\n  camera.fov = THREE.MathUtils.lerp(f0, f1, smooth(fu));\n  camera.updateProjectionMatrix();\n\n  // subtle handheld breath\n  camera.position.y += Math.sin(t * 1.7) * 0.12;\n  camera.rotation.z += Math.sin(t * 0.9) * 0.0018;\n\n  // title cues\n  cue('titleIn',  t > 1.0,  () => $('titleMain').classList.add('visible'));\n  cue('titleOut', t > 6.0,  () => $('titleMain').classList.remove('visible'));\n  cue('endIn',    t > 16.8, () => $('titleEnd').classList.add('visible'));\n  cue('endOut',   t > T - 0.4, () => $('titleEnd').classList.remove('visible'));\n}\n\n$('playBtn').addEventListener('click', startShowcase);\n\n/* ================================================================\n   MAIN LOOP\n   ================================================================ */\nconst clock = new THREE.Clock();\nfunction animate() {\n  requestAnimationFrame(animate);\n  const dt = Math.min(clock.getDelta(), 0.05);\n  const t = clock.elapsedTime;\n\n  // birds\n  for (const b of birds) {\n    const u = b.userData;\n    const a = t * u.speed + u.phase;\n    b.position.set(Math.cos(a) * u.r, u.h + Math.sin(a * 2.3) * 3, -120 + Math.sin(a) * u.r);\n    b.lookAt(\n      Math.cos(a + 0.05) * u.r,\n      u.h + Math.sin((a + 0.05) * 2.3) * 3,\n      -120 + Math.sin(a + 0.05) * u.r\n    );\n    const flap = Math.sin(t * u.flap + u.phase) * 0.7;\n    u.wl.rotation.z = flap;\n    u.wr.rotation.z = -flap;\n  }\n\n  if (showcase.playing) updateShowcase(dt);\n  else if (fly.active) updateFly(dt);\n  else controls.update();\n\n  renderer.render